update-node-alternatives (0.4.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * calc_priority: include the patch number. The priority was major *
    100 + minor, so two patch releases of the same minor (v22.22.1 and
    v22.22.2) tied and auto mode did not reliably pick the newest. It is
    now major * 1000000 + minor * 1000 + patch (v22.14.0 -> 22014000),
    within update-alternatives' 32-bit range up to v2147.
  * postinst: on upgrade from a version older than 0.4.2, re-register
    the installed Node.js versions with the new priorities. The manual
    selection, if any, is kept.
  * Document the new formula in the man page, the six READMEs and
    AGENTS.md; tests cover patch ordering in auto mode.

 -- Eric Lemesre <eric.lemesre@gmail.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 10:36:43 +0100

update-node-alternatives (0.4.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Run npm with the node of its own version. The global-package
    migration called <version>/bin/npm, a '#!/usr/bin/env node' script,
    so it ran under whichever node came first in PATH: the active one
    (wrong ABI for native modules) or none at all under a sudo
    secure_path without /usr/local/bin ('env: node: No such file or
    directory'). New helper npm_for() prepends the version's bin/ to
    PATH.
  * Prepend /usr/local/bin to PATH when it is missing, so npm --version,
    --promote-user-globals and --cleanup-user-globals also work under a
    restricted sudo secure_path. 'sudo -u <user> npm config get prefix'
    now forwards PATH as well.
  * do_update: keep the manual selection. It ran
    'update-alternatives --remove-all node' before re-registering every
    version, which silently switched the group back to auto mode
    (highest version) on every --install, --update and
    --promote-user-globals.
  * --set: read the previously active version before do_update. It was
    read afterwards, so the migration offered the packages of the
    highest installed version instead of those of the version being
    replaced.
  * migrate_global_packages: say so when there is nothing to migrate
    instead of printing nothing outside --verbose.
  * Add tests/functional.sh and a 'make test' target, run by
    dh_auto_test: sandboxed update-alternatives, fake Node.js versions,
    sudo-like PATH without /usr/local/bin. No root and no network
    needed.

 -- Eric Lemesre <eric.lemesre@gmail.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 10:22:00 +0100

update-node-alternatives (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  [ Phase 1 -- Debian standards alignment + rename ]
  * Rename source and binary package: update-node-alternative ->
    update-node-alternatives. The trailing 's' aligns with
    update-alternatives(1), which the wrapper extends. Renames the
    script, its man page, the package data directory
    (/usr/share/update-node-alternatives/), and updates Homepage,
    Vcs-* URLs in debian/control. There is no transitional package:
    the old name was never published.
  * debconf scenario 1.b. New templates ask, at first install:
    - which Node.js version to install by default (latest LTS / latest /
      none / custom); default 'none' so DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive
      never silently downloads binaries;
    - whether 'apt purge' should later wipe /usr/local/share/nvm/.
    The purge-nvm-store answer is re-confirmed at purge time so the
    admin sees the current default before /usr/local/share/nvm/ is
    deleted. Pre-Depends on debconf (>= 0.5) | debconf-2.0,
    Build-Depends on po-debconf.
  * debian/manpages: hand the man page to dh_installman for compression
    and permissions. The Makefile gains an INSTALL_MAN flag (default 1)
    that debian/rules sets to 0 so make install behaviour is unchanged
    out-of-package.
  * debian/upstream/metadata: list Repository, Repository-Browse,
    Bug-Database and Bug-Submit URLs (DEP-12, lintian suggestion).
  * debian/README.Debian: document the package contract -- why
    dh_installalternatives is not used (alternative targets are created
    at runtime under /usr/local/share/nvm/), and how the purge policy
    works.

  [ Phase 1bis -- debconf translations ]
  * Add po-debconf translations for the top ~10 locales by activity on
    i18n.debian.org: fr (hand-reviewed), de, es, it, pt_BR, nl, ru,
    ja, cs, sv (machine drafts -- intended as a starting point for the
    debian-l10n-<lang> lists once the package is published). All ten
    files validate with msgfmt -c.

  [ Phase 2 -- dynamic slaves, profile.d, completion, per-user globals ]
  * Dynamic slaves. do_update() no longer relies on a fixed
    CORE_BINARIES=(npm npx corepack) list. Each --install / --set /
    --auto / --update now scans <version>/bin/ and registers every
    executable other than `node` as a slave alternative. Binaries
    deposited by `sudo npm install -g` (ng, tsc, pnpm, ...) become
    /usr/local/bin/<name> symlinks managed by update-alternatives(1)
    without further script changes. node_binaries.info gains
    Binaries.<version>=... lines while the union Binaries=... line is
    preserved for backward compatibility.
  * postrm: reads the union from node_binaries.info on `apt purge` so
    dynamic slaves are removed cleanly; falls back to the static
    `node npm npx corepack` set if the state file is gone.
  * /etc/profile.d/update-node-alternatives.sh: defaults
    NPM_CONFIG_PREFIX to $HOME/.npm-global on login (POSIX sh,
    idempotent) and prefixes $NPM_CONFIG_PREFIX/bin to PATH. Combined
    with dynamic slaves, this lets a regular user override a system-
    wide binary by running `npm i -g <pkg>` without sudo, with PATH
    order alone arbitrating which binary wins. Makefile gains a
    PROFILED variable (default /etc/profile.d, absolute, not under
    PREFIX).
  * Bash completion. New bash-completion/update-node-alternatives,
    installed at /usr/share/bash-completion/completions/update-node-
    alternatives. Completes the long/short option list, installed
    versions for --remove/--set/--list-packages/--from/--to, valid
    frontends for --frontend, and hints common LTS aliases for
    --install/--upgrade.
  * --promote-user-globals (root via sudo, refuses without $SUDO_USER):
    discovers the user's npm prefix via `sudo -u $SUDO_USER -H npm
    config get prefix`, lists per-user `npm install -g` packages not
    yet covered system-wide at >= the per-user version, checklists
    the rest, then re-installs the selection in the system-wide layer
    with `HOME=/root npm install -g` (the user's .npmrc, registry and
    tokens are NEVER inherited for the root install). Calls --update
    so the freshly installed binaries become alternatives. Optionally
    chains into --cleanup-user-globals via `exec sudo -u $SUDO_USER`.
  * --cleanup-user-globals (user only, refuses if id -u == 0). Drops
    every per-user `npm install -g` package whose system-wide
    counterpart is at >= version, via `npm uninstall -g`. Idempotent:
    never strands the user on a feature only their per-user copy
    carries.
  * Decision: no automatic post-`npm install -g` hook is shipped (the
    simplest of the three options weighed in ToDo.md).
    `update-node-alternatives --update` is the documented re-sync
    entry point; the man page now says so explicitly.
  * docs: update-node-alternatives(8) gains a Per-user override
    subsection, a Per-user globals action subsection, EXAMPLES for
    `npm i -g` + --update, --promote-user-globals and
    --cleanup-user-globals, FILES entries for /etc/profile.d/, the
    bash-completion script and the new node_binaries.info schema, and
    ENVIRONMENT entries for NPM_CONFIG_PREFIX and SUDO_USER.
    README.md / README.fr.md mirror the new feature surface.

 -- Eric Lemesre <eric.lemesre@gmail.com>  Sat, 09 May 2026 22:18:47 +0200

update-node-alternative (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
    - Manage system-wide Node.js versions via NVM and update-alternatives.
    - Interactive debconf-style frontend (whiptail/dialog) with readline
      fallback via --no-dialog.
    - Actions: --install, --remove, --list, --list-remote, --set, --auto,
      --update, --list-packages, --upgrade, --reinstall-packages.
    - Interactive migration of global npm packages between versions.
    - Ships a manual page (update-node-alternative(8)).
    - Bundles nvm 0.40.4, advertised via Provides: bundled-nvm-0.40.4.
    - Tracks upstream releases via debian/watch (uscan), including the
      embedded nvm component.
    - Honours DEBIAN_FRONTEND (debconf(7)): adds gnome (zenity), kde
      (kdialog) and noninteractive frontends in addition to the existing
      whiptail/dialog and readline ones. Adds --frontend NAME to force
      a specific backend; --no-dialog is now an alias of
      --frontend=readline. zenity and kdialog are listed under Suggests.
    - Drop the obsolete install-node-alternative.sh helper. Replaced by
      `make install` (script + man + vendored nvm) and a new `make purge`
      target for the manual install path. Per-user nvm migration is
      documented in the README.
    - postrm: on purge, remove the update-alternatives entries for
      node/npm/npx/corepack registered at runtime by the script.
    - Refresh the package long description to mention the new frontends.

 -- Eric Lemesre <eric.lemesre@gmail.com>  Wed, 29 Apr 2026 13:41:57 +0200
